## Context

The existing #PROMOTED/#DELETED mismatch is a compatibility defect, not a justification to tombstone every generalised source. Narrow this ticket to the legacy reader/import mapping required by the portable migration.

Design baseline: v7. v6 was merged by PR #903 and is frozen at `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-v6.md`; v7 closes the acceptance review's four §12.1 conditions and settles the nomenclature, leaving the architecture and this ticket's scope unchanged. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`, `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-nomenclature.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

`skills/dream/provenance.py` live-body walker; existing marker stubs; schema/import API selected in 0911.

## Actions

1. Enumerate legacy markers and distinguish actual inactive stubs from substantive local observations.
2. Map verified inactive records to explicit v7 lifecycle and replacement references where known; report ambiguous promotion semantics for review.
3. Provide an import result used by 0920. Do not run the old promotion algorithm or rewrite the entire corpus.

## Test

Fixtures cover both legacy markers, an active particular with a generalises relationship, and an ambiguous stub. Both known inactive markers are excluded; the particular stays active; ambiguity is reported.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v7, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Legacy mapping and ambiguity report are available to the migration.
- [ ] Reader/writer status contract agrees; generalisation does not imply inactivity.
- [ ] No count-based assertion or automatic project-copy retirement remains.
